  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Waste Gas-to-Ethanol Conversion, through LanzaTech, Inc.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A USTDA grant is partially funding a feasibility study to assess the technical and economic viability of implementing a proprietary gas fermentation process to convert waste gases into industrial-grade ethanol at a ferrochrome production plant near Middleburg in the South African province of Mpumalanga (Project). The Grantee is Swayana (Pty) Ltd, a project developer based in Johannesburg, South Africa. The Study is being undertaken by LanzaTech, Inc. of Sokokie, IL. The results of the Study will help attract additional investment to the Project and support the scale-up of this U.S. technology in South Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
